# OpticWise SB7 BrandScript Rule

Whenever you are asked to write, edit, reposition, draft, or proof anything that represents **OpticWise (OW)** — externally or internally — follow the OW SB7 BrandScript canon **except where this rule explicitly carves out paths or channels**.

## Scope — where SB7 is compulsory vs excluded (this `opticwise-html` repo)

- **SB7 compulsory:** All site pages **except** HTML living under `insights/` and `faq/`. Treat these as the canonical marketing and narrative surface.
- **SB7 not compulsory:** `insights/**` (Insight / long-form posts) and `faq/**`. Do not run SB7 rewrites, banned-word scrubs, or checklist enforcement on those files unless the user explicitly asks. Preserve author and source text, citations, and link targets (including SEO / outbound link strategy). The word **PropTech** may appear when naming third-party outlets, anchor text, or quoted coverage.
- **Still true everywhere (including insights and FAQ):** Do **not** describe **OpticWise** as "PropTech." Never invent client names, metrics, quotes, case studies, or proof points.

**All other OW outputs** (LinkedIn, decks, emails, board materials, pages on other properties, etc.) remain under full SB7 unless a brief says otherwise.

**Read the connected canon before writing a single word** (for work in SB7 scope):

@OW_SB7_brandscript.md

The connected file is the synthesized brandscript canon — SB7 narrative, voice, trademarks, banned words, PPP 5C™ plan, two-layer model, asset-manager mindset overlay, approved Wins & Nightmares, Big Three Plays diagnostic, NOI benchmarks, market-context thesis, sales reframes, competitive posture, and pre-publish checklist. For **non-excluded** work, it overrides anything in this codebase that contradicts it.

**Acronyms (define on request, never substitute):**
- **OW** = OpticWise
- **PPP** = Peak Property Performance®

